    "title": "Is Solo Ball related to Lonzo, LaMelo Ball? How UConn star fits into March Madness compared to Ball brothers",
    "text": "Subscribe to Yahoo Fantasy ForecastApple Podcasts | Spotify | YouTubeDraft week is finally upon us and we have finally reached the final pod before the big even gets going. Matt Harmon and Justin Boone wishcast (don't call it a mock!) their favorite fantasy landing spots for the top QB, RB, WR and TE prospects in this year's draft class. The two, within reason, place the prospects in the best spots for them to become instant fantasy contributors in 2026.Advertisement(3:00) - Programming note: Live Draft shows on Thursday and Friday + Recap pod on Saturday(5:00) - RB favorite landing spots: Jeremiyah Love, Jadarian Price, Mike Washington Jr.(24:20) - RB favorite landing spots: Jonah Coleman, Nicholas Singleton, Kaytron Allen, Emmett Johnson(37:40) - WR favorite landing spots: Jordyn Tyson, Makai Lemon, Carnell Tate, KC Concepcion, Denzel Boston(56:45) - WR favorite landing spots: Omar Cooper Jr., Elijah Sarratt, Chris Bell, Chris Brazzell, Germie Bernard, Malachi Fields(1:13:00) - QB favorite landing spots: Fernando Mendoza, Ty Simpson, Garrett Nussmeier, Drew AllarAdvertisement(1:22:40) - TE favorite landing spots: Kenyon Sadiq + Eli StowersDraft week is finally upon us and we have finally reached the final pod before the big even gets going. Matt Harmon and Justin Boone wishcast (don't call it a mock!) their favorite fantasy landing spots for the top QB, RB, WR and TE prospects in this year's draft class. The two, within reason, place the prospects in the best spots for them to become instant fantasy contributors in 2026. (Jason Jung)🖥️ Watch this full episode on YouTubeCheck out all episodes of the Yahoo Fantasy Forecast and the rest of the Yahoo Sports podcast family at https://apple.co/3zEuTQj or at yahoosports.tv",
